				\begin{document}$${{B}}_{\max }=\frac{{{B}}_{0}\times {\text{IC}}_{50}}{[{L}]}$$\end{document}Bmax=B0×IC50[L]in which B0 represents the total specific binding and [L] is the ligand concentration. The equilibrium dissociation constant (Kd) was obtained with the equation51:\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
